'''Transhumanism''' is a political and philosophical movement that advocates the [[wikipedia:human enhancement|enhancement of the human condition]] by developing and making widely available new and future technologies to enhance longevity, cognition, and well-being. It rose in prominence in early-24th-century [[Visala]]. Transhumanism is characterized by support for [[wikipedia:eugenics|eugenics]], [[wikipedia:natalism|natalism]], [[wikipedia:reactionary modernism|reactionary modernism]] and [[wikipedia:Technological utopianism|technological utopianism]]. Opposed to [[wikipedia:Bioconservatism|bioconservatism]], [[wikipedia:neo-Luddism|neo-Luddism]] and [[wikipedia:liberalism|liberalism]], transhumanism is generally considered on the far-right of the traditional left–right spectrum, although that positioning is debated by scholars. 

